% expect-output: 9.44
% expect-output: 0.0
% divergence: resident-inventory
% Scenario: re-encoding changes widths. A copy of Helvetica whose
% Encoding maps code 65 to /W keeps the resident marker, so (A) measures
% as W (944 units) at size 10.
% Expect: 9.44 and 0.0.
/r { 1000 mul round 1000 div } def
/Helvetica findfont dup length dict copy
dup /Encoding get 256 array copy dup 65 /W put
1 index exch /Encoding exch put
/H2 exch definefont pop
/H2 findfont 10 scalefont setfont
(A) stringwidth r exch r = =
